# Finding 12 — the tab strip still gives no ` +N hidden ` count when it
# overflows, and labels still clip. The chip exists (ui/bufferline.zig)
# but only paints when the strip is scrolled to a tail that fits whole;
# in the ordinary overflow case (the active tab cut at the right edge)
# it never renders. The `<` `>` arrows DO paint and are clickable now,
# so the overflow is no longer completely silent.
# 12 buffers at 120x40 — the Rust strip shows `+N hidden` here.
# width: 120
# height: 40
write file01name.txt x
write file02name.txt x
write file03name.txt x
write file04name.txt x
write file05name.txt x
write file06name.txt x
write file07name.txt x
write file08name.txt x
write file09name.txt x
write file10name.txt x
write file11name.txt x
write file12name.txt x
open file01name.txt
open file02name.txt
open file03name.txt
open file04name.txt
open file05name.txt
open file06name.txt
open file07name.txt
open file08name.txt
open file09name.txt
open file10name.txt
open file11name.txt
open file12name.txt
expect screen contains "file12name.txt"
expect screen contains " hidden "
